\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Group-algebra sectors}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{How can the same half-turn act on different Gaussian states?
The [group-algebra extension](fdip-003N) and its
[module projectors](fdip-003O) separate the
[actual half-turn sectors](fdip-000L) whenever two is invertible.
The action and its projectors are specified before a probability
law is attached. [Support parity and sign sectors](fdip-003P)
are different decompositions of the same fields.}

\p{Over the reals, an orthogonal involution commuting with positive
precision gives a [product law](fdip-000M); the
[four-cycle calculation](fdip-003S) computes its two blocks and retained
marginals. Symmetry still permits [mixing within a sector](fdip-003T),
and in [characteristic two](fdip-000N) the action survives without the
complementary projectors. These examples separate the supplied symmetry,
the coefficient assumptions and the choice of state.}

\transclude{fdip-003N}
